Violence broke out as thousands of protesters gathered in the Philippine capital Manila on September 21, 2025. The demonstrators were venting their anger about a ballooning scandal involving a flood control project that is believed to have cost taxpayers billions of dollars. Rage over the so-called ghost infrastructure projects has been mounting in the Southeast Asian country since President Ferdinand Marcos Jnr put them centre stage in a July state of the nation address after weeks of deadly flooding. Dozens of people have been arrested and scores were hurt in clashes with police.
